From 3cc4a1bc5d7d2c49f04e460101a67123c8fc4ee9 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: t <tristan75015@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 13 Oct 2026 16:45:48 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] Documentation: review of the pages and comments changed by
 the prototype

The pages of docs/ and the comments of the headers and sources added or
changed by the prototype were checked against the code (84 findings, 78
fixed here, the others being code defects left for later):

- checkVariableExistence: the meaning of the two members of the result was
  inverted;
- configuration files: where they are installed and searched, including
  the mismatch with TFEL_APPEND_SUFFIX;
- generic-parallel interface: statistics of the stlpar and openmp backends
  during rotations, hip-clang on AMD GPUs, sycl-gpu-acpp, accessibility of
  the pointers by memory space, single-pass compilers (nvc++, generic
  AdaptiveCpp) which follow the device branches on the host too;
- TFEL_STATIC_VARIABLE (copies of the static variables of the code blocks)
  in tfel-config.md, in the behaviours page and in the release notes;
- release notes 5.2: rkCastem using the Young modulus again, DDIF2 fixes,
  use_stress_update_algorithm with @UseQt, findSingleEigenValue aborting on
  the host; bounds_status of the generic material properties, DTAU_DDF
  operator of the generic behaviours, typos (AdaptiveCpp, nvc++, msg field
  of OutputStatus).

No code is changed: the sources without their comments are identical.
